From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Matthew Feickert <matthew.feickert@cern.ch>
Date: Mon, 23 Nov 2026 15:09:09 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] Do not insert into the hash table inside assert

map_quadrilaterals inserts each internal edge of the triangulation into
the e2q hash table inside an assert, which also checks that the key is
unique:

    assert(ht_insert(e2q, &key, q) == NULL);

When NDEBUG is defined, assert expands to nothing, so the edges are
never inserted. The later ht_find then returns NULL and q1->id
dereferences it, crashing for every boundary whose triangulation has
more than one quadrilateral. conda-forge builds on Windows with
-DNDEBUG in CFLAGS, while upstream's makefile does not define it.

Call ht_insert unconditionally and only assert on its result. No other
assert in gridgen's sources has a side effect.
---
 gridgen/gridgen.c | 5 ++++-
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/gridgen/gridgen.c b/gridgen/gridgen.c
index 163a451..2e6b0e7 100644
--- a/gridgen/gridgen.c
+++ b/gridgen/gridgen.c
@@ -2159,6 +2159,7 @@ static void map_quadrilaterals(gridgen* gg)
     for (i = 0; i < nq; ++i) {
         quadrilateral* q = &gg->quadrilaterals[i];
         int key[2];
+        void* existing;
 
         if (q->vids[0] < q->vids[2]) {
             key[0] = q->vids[0];
@@ -2171,7 +2172,9 @@ static void map_quadrilaterals(gridgen* gg)
         /*
          * make sure that the edge generates a unique key
          */
-        assert(ht_insert(e2q, &key, q) == NULL);
+        existing = ht_insert(e2q, &key, q);
+        assert(existing == NULL);
+        (void) existing;
     }
 
     /*
